# 2026-11-09 cloud seat (Claude Opus 5.5), floor lane, PREDICTION seat. PRE-RUN freeze, prediction first. Integer/rational only, HBP; no JSON.
# Object: a rigorous, unconditional, lift-free lower bound gamma_cert on lambda_min(QHQ) (H/J_E = 72 I - T + r M on the 2,177,317,873 gauge orbits of the periodic 3x4 S3 lattice, Q = nonflat) at r = 9, by the Schur-Collatz-Wielandt certificate (Theorem S, design/NOTE.md section 2).
# Nothing that depends on r was computed for the 3x4 model at r = 9, or at any r with |r - 9| <= 1, by this lane before these rows, except the one critic run at r = 90000001/10000000 disclosed in row 093 (values withheld, not recorded). Every computation of the lane is disclosed in rows 085-102 and 104-109 (row 109 pre-lists the folder of the records verifier of this file).
# Row types: FREEZE (the frozen run), PIN (a pinned hash), REQUIRED (a gate the r = 9 run and its report must pass), PREDICT (a prediction), STATUS (read-and-report status of another lane's result), LINK (the link to the #137 package), DISCLOSE (a pre-freeze computation).
# Tags: DERIVED (proved in design/NOTE.md or by the review seat), CONJECTURE (a frozen prediction, falsifiable by the r = 9 run), REPORTED (from another PR, lane or seat), OPEN (not known before the run), REQUIRED (a rule). basis=MEASURED marks r-independent counts or excluded-r smoke only.
# Every row carries id, quantity, value, tag, met_if, not_met_if and falsifier. A colon in a quoted output line (GATE:name:PASS) stands for the pipe of that line. Paths are relative to the package root (the folder that holds final/ and work/, at any absolute location; in version 1 it was scratchpad/floor/) unless they start with ../.
# Notation used in the rules: g0 = 94070673/1000000 (#131's floor, REPORTED); G(m) = the largest gamma among the r = 9 certificates at m0 = m that pass every REQUIRED row; U(m) = the smallest Ritz upper bound (writer ritz_upper or verifier RITZ_CLASS_VECTOR, each plus 1/1000000 for truncation) among those certificates; U_all = min of U(m) over the steps run; gamma_cert = max of G(m) over the steps run.
# This file is the input whose sha256 is compiled into the frozen binary (FLOORCERT_PREDICTION_SHA256). It must not be edited after that hash is taken. design/NOTE.md, CHANGES.txt and the companion NOTE-S3-3X4-R9-FLOOR-CERT-20261109.md carry the prose; this file is authoritative.
# VERSION 2 (2026-11-10, local build seat, Claude Opus 5.5). This file follows an operational review of version 1, the freeze commit e74d8a46e86034096fd9c9231c87f594f17a93bf (prediction sha256 d06ff237f55a762e7c50087d98a757ed366e749f6a736c9c1793f495efd84041), which stays unchanged as the historical prediction-first record. Version 2 carries the blind history of version 1 and adds none: the near-9 critic run of row 093 stays disclosed, and rows 110-114 disclose the review, its errata E1-E5 and everything run for version 2.
# Version 2 changes rows 001 003 006 007 008 009 010 013 016 020 070 and adds rows 110-122; rows 006 007 008 keep every version 1 byte and gain one v2_launch field; the other 98 rows are byte-identical to version 1 (review-v1/ROW-COMPARE-V1-V2.hbp). Every PREDICT row keeps its value, met_if, not_met_if and falsifier; row 070 changes one memory figure in its basis field. No r = 9 value and no value at r within 1 of 9 was computed for version 2.
# CORRECTION ROUND (2026-11-10, same seat): one commit on top of the first version 2 commit cfc57befadcb61fb36b992af841941adaecd3fd0. It applies the reviewer's rulings and the findings of the separate verifier seat to the launcher and its evaluator (rows 114-117 and 119-122): the launcher runs private hashed copies of the gate and verifier tools, and a completed process at or over 2097152 kB gives CERTIFICATE=FAIL with RESOURCE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED and no fallback. The Rust source, the binary hash of row 016 and the 16 PREDICT rows are byte-identical to that commit. The launcher's last line reads FLOOR_RUN|CERTIFICATE=...|PREDICTION=...|DECISION=...|GAMMA=...|UPPER_BOUND=...|...|HASHES=...; the r = 9 mode starts only with the token --launch-r9 and stays on HOLD.
